# Programs of this corpus whose output is not a function of this tree.
# One basename per line, each with the reason -- where the program gets
# what this tree cannot supply, named specifically enough that a later
# reader can go and look.
#
# The entry says what a difference may be read as, not what any two
# runs will be. A program that draws on the clock is free to give the
# same answer twice, and how often it does is a property of the machine
# rather than of the tree, so nothing here is measured by rendering the
# program again and seeing whether it moved: a check like that reports
# the machine's jitter and reddens on a run that found none. What the
# entry rests on is the reason below it, and the corpus fails for an
# entry that carries none -- a bare name excuses every difference the
# program ever shows and says nothing about why, which is the one thing
# it was for.
#
# This is a narrower thing than differing from another engine. A
# program that seeds a generator with a constant renders the same page
# in this tree every time and a different one elsewhere: the PLRM gives
# rand a range and an srand/rrand interface and says nothing about the
# sequence between them (PLRM 8.2, rand), so two conforming engines are
# free to draw different figures from one seed. That difference is
# between engines and this register is not about it. snowflak is
# exactly that program and is deliberately not named here.
#
# vasarely -- seeds the generator from usertime: the program opens with
#             "usertime srand" and every colour, angle and figure on
#             the page follows from the seed. usertime is the execution
#             the interpreter has had, in milliseconds (PLRM 8.2,
#             usertime), so the seed is however many milliseconds of
#             work booting and reading this far happened to take, which
#             is the machine's answer and not the tree's. Holding
#             usertime to a constant makes two runs byte-identical and
#             changing that constant changes the page, so it is the
#             whole of the difference.
vasarely
